---
/** Slide 06 · The receipts — the doctrine already works here. */
---

<section data-slot="06" data-variant="awm-p1" class="deck-section">
  <span class="deck-kicker">06 / 09</span>

  <div>
    <p class="deck-eyebrow mb-3">The receipts</p>
    <h2 class="deck-h2">
      The mega-gifts landscape scan <em>was</em> the doctrine in action:
      <span class="deck-gradient">84 verified gifts, 81 sources, one afternoon.</span>
    </h2>
  </div>

  <div class="deck-grid mt-2" style="grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(230px, 1fr));">
    <div class="deck-card flex flex-col gap-2">
      <span class="deck-stat" style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 3.6vw, 3rem);">84</span>
      <p style="color: var(--color-text-muted); font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.1vw, 1.2rem); line-height: 1.5; margin: 0;">verified gifts across six topic lanes — parallel research agents, primary-source verification.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="deck-card flex flex-col gap-2">
      <span class="deck-stat" style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 3.6vw, 3rem);">185+</span>
      <p style="color: var(--color-text-muted); font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.1vw, 1.2rem); line-height: 1.5; margin: 0;">sources in a hex-coded citation registry — every number in every pitch deck traceable.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="deck-card flex flex-col gap-2">
      <span class="deck-stat" style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 3.6vw, 3rem);">8</span>
      <p style="color: var(--color-text-muted); font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.1vw, 1.2rem); line-height: 1.5; margin: 0;">strategy pitch decks built on that evidence base — including this one.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="deck-lede mt-2" style="max-width: 70ch;">
    The doctrine isn't hypothetical: it's how the evidence under every one of
    these pitch decks was assembled — at a speed and coverage no manual pass
    achieves.
  </p>
</section>
